    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d313">

                <pb facs="0259" n="209" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg209"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.77/227</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chairman of the Advisory Commission of Railway
                        Experts to Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Stevens</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Harbin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" notAfter="1917-11-24T16:05:00-05:00"
                            notBefore="1917-11-23T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received
                            November 24, 1917, 4.05 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>For Willard:</p>
                <p>Just reached Harbin to meet Emerson. Cable me quick Harbin, care of the United
                    States Consul, what ship and when it is due Vladivostok. Send Emerson wireless
                    not to land until I advise him as conditions may not make it advisable. Cable me
                    latest reliable news from St. Petersburg; have nothing from there for twelve
                    days, then situation desperate all over Russia looked like civil war. Quiet
                    through Siberia but may change any day. Siberian Railroad chief meets me here
                    quickly (?) to watch situation and decide matters. I have telegraphed Francis to
                    send Horn<anchor n="1" xml:id="d313-f1"/> to Caucasus.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stevens</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d313-f1" n="1" xml:id="d313-f1-content">
                <p>Henry J. Horn, member of the Advisory Commission of Railway Experts, to
                    Russia.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
